<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ProjectGuid>{d7a2e1f3-8c4b-4e9d-b5a6-3f1c2d8e7a9b}</ProjectGuid>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);xUnit1051</NoWarn>
    <!-- 🚨 DO NOT re-add <ConcurrentGarbageCollection>false</ConcurrentGarbageCollection> here.
         #1274 set it, reasoning that this project's recurring `exit=139` was a null MethodTable in
         `WKS::gc_heap::background_sweep()` and that `background_sweep` only runs with background GC
         enabled. Two core dumps from the window AFTER it merged (runs 31590331741 and 31597122789,
         runtime 10.0.11) fault at the identical instruction — `mov ecx,[rax]` with `RAX=0`, i.e. a
         MethodTable pointer of zero — inside `WKS::gc_heap::plan_phase(int)`, which is the
         stop-the-world plan step of a BLOCKING collection and runs whether or not concurrent GC is
         on. So the mechanism the property targets is not the one firing, the measured CI rate did not
         move (4.2% -> 3.8%), and leaving it reads as "GC was already ruled out" when nothing was.
         Full evidence: Doc/Architecture/DebuggingNativeCrashes -> "2026-08-12". Issue #613. -->
  </PropertyGroup>

